{"name":"Holy Crow","hex":"#332f2c","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holy crow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A mild oath."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holy_crow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crow","blocks":[{"text":"A crow is a bird of the genus Corvus, or more broadly, a synonym for all of Corvus. The word \"crow\" is used as part of the common name of many species. The related term \"raven\" is not linked scientifically to any certain trait but is rather a general grouping for larger-sized species of Corvus. The collective name for a group of crows is a \"murder\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Corvus_corone_-near_Canford_Cliffs%2C_Poole%2C_England-8.jpg/330px-Corvus_corone_-near_Canford_Cliffs%2C_Poole%2C_England-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Corvus_corone_-near_Canford_Cliffs%2C_Poole%2C_England-8.jpg/500px-Corvus_corone_-near_Canford_Cliffs%2C_Poole%2C_England-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Corvus_corone_-near_Canford_Cliffs%2C_Poole%2C_England-8.jpg/500px-Corvus_corone_-near_Canford_Cliffs%2C_Poole%2C_England-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A carrion crow scavenging on a beach in Dorset, England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorvus_corone_-near_Canford_Cliffs%2C_Poole%2C_England-8.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}